    /// <remarks>
    ///   <para>owl:Class</para>
    ///   <para>"Cells are originally plated at a certain concentration referred to as seeding density. Upon a first passage this primary culture becomes a secondary cell culture that can be propagated to become a stable and homogneous cell line. This class covers establishment of primary cultures from any native cell - 'in vivo' cells isolated from some multicellular organism, or 'in environment' unicellular organisms isolated from some natural environment."^^&lt;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string&gt;</para>
